{
    "background_story": "Juan was a former construction worker from a small village in Spain. Growing up, he was always fascinated by the strongmen who performed at local festivals, lifting massive weights and bending steel bars. Juan spent years training in secret, honing his strength and technique in the village quarry. His big break came when he was discovered by a talent scout, who invited him to compete in the World's Strongest Man competition. Juan's impressive physique and incredible feats of strength, including lifting a 400-pound boulder and breaking a chain with his bare hands, earned him the nickname 'El Toro' (The Bull). He went on to win the competition three years in a row, becoming a national hero and an inspiration to aspiring strongmen around the world.",
